  "performance": {"required": true, "baselineFactor": 10},
  "hints": ["Four numbers are enough, updated town by town: the lowest cost of a first load, the best gain after one deal, the lowest cost of a second load, and the best gain after two deals.", "The real cost of a second load is its price MINUS the gain already made with the first deal. That is what ties the two deals together.", "Start the costs at 999999 and the gains at 0. For each price: the first cost is the MIN of itself and the price; the first gain the MAX of itself and price MINUS first cost; the second cost the MIN of itself and price MINUS first gain; the second gain the MAX of itself and price MINUS second cost. RETURN the second gain."],
